`progress` written with no `value` is indeterminate: a bar that says work is
happening and not how much is left. Zero is a legitimate fraction and cannot
double as "not known", so `value` is an `option<float>` and the absence is in
the type -- which is also the only way an override can ask whether a call site
supplied it at all.

Each platform answers in its own shape, and the two halves of each pair are
here together so the difference is visible:

  html      `<progress>` with no `value` attribute is the browser's own
            indeterminate bar. The absence is spelled by leaving the attribute
            off rather than by choosing a number to stand for "unknown".
  android   Compose splits determinate from indeterminate by whether the
            `progress` argument is there, so the override writes the two calls.
  gtk4      GTK spells indeterminate as repeated gtk_progress_bar_pulse()
            calls rather than as a property, and an override has no clock to
            drive them, so the bar is empty.
  bubbletea bubbles' progress is a fraction with no indeterminate mode; the
            bar is empty and `spinner` is the widget that says "working".
  fyne      the bar is a Label stub, so it shows its `label` instead of a
            number it does not have.

The determinate half also pins two things the `option` made necessary. Compose
takes `() -> Float`, so the intrinsic declares a func prop returning `float32`
and the emitter writes Kotlin's anonymous-function literal -- `fun(): Float`
states both the return type inference would have got wrong and the `return`
a lambda cannot carry. And the fraction still folds to a constant through the
option: `float(option<float>(2.0)) / 10.0` is 0.2 before any target sees it.

deny out/none/html/index.html `value=""` -- an absent value leaves the attribute off; it is not an empty one
deny out/kotlin/android/app/src/main/java/test/sngl/app/MainScreen.kt `null` -- both call sites are settled at build time, so no null test and no nullable Double survive into Kotlin
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `set_fraction\(.* / ` -- the fraction folds to a constant; cgo is handed a number, not a division to do
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `snglSome` -- a value put into an option and read straight back out is neither boxed nor dereferenced
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        gtk4(gir="builtin")
        bubbletea
        fyne
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
    none {
        html
    }
}

window(title="t") {
    progress(value=2.0, max=10.0)
    progress(label="working")
}
